Subtask 3.5: Test Windows Credential
Create a Windows test playbook:

Create a new job template for Windows testing
Use the following playbook content:
---
- name: Test Windows Machine Credential
  hosts: windows
  gather_facts: yes
  tasks:
    - name: Check Windows system information
      win_shell: |
        Write-Output "Computer: $env:COMPUTERNAME"
        Write-Output "OS: $(Get-WmiObject -Class Win32_OperatingSystem | Select-Object -ExpandProperty Caption)"
        Write-Output "PowerShell Version: $($PSVersionTable.PSVersion.Major).$($PSVersionTable.PSVersion.Minor)"
      register: system_info
    
    - name: Display system information
      debug:
        msg: "{{ system_info.stdout_lines }}"
    
    - name: Test file creation
      win_file:
        path: C:\temp\ansible_test.txt
        state: touch
      register: file_result
    
    - name: Display file creation result
      debug:
        msg: "File creation successful: {{ file_result.changed }}"
    
    - name: Test service query
      win_service_info:
        name: Spooler
      register: service_info
    
    - name: Display service status
      debug:
        msg: "Print Spooler service status: {{ service_info.services[0].state }}"
    
    - name: Clean up test file
      win_file:
        path: C:\temp\ansible_test.txt
        state: absent
Task 4: Advanced Credential Management
Subtask 4.1: Using Credential Variables
Create dynamic credentials using variables:

---
- name: Dynamic Credential Usage
  hosts: all
  vars:
    ansible_user: "{{ credential_username }}"
    ansible_ssh_private_key_file: "{{ credential_ssh_key }}"
  tasks:
    - name: Display current user
      debug:
        msg: "Running as user: {{ ansible_user }}"
Subtask 4.2: Credential Security Best Practices
Rotate credentials regularly:
# Script to rotate SSH keys
#!/bin/bash
# Generate new key
ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -f ~/.ssh/ansible_key_new

# Update authorized_keys on targets
ansible all -m authorized_key -a "user=ansible key='{{ lookup('file', '~/.ssh/ansible_key_new.pub') }}' state=present"

# Update credential in Controller
# (This would be done through the web interface)
Use vault for sensitive data:
# Create encrypted vault file
ansible-vault create group_vars/all/vault.yml
# Content of vault.yml
vault_windows_password: "SecureP@ssw0rd123!"
vault_ssh_key_passphrase: "MySecurePassphrase"
Subtask 4.3: Testing Multiple Credentials
Create a comprehensive test playbook:

---
- name: Comprehensive Credential Test
  hosts: all
  gather_facts: yes
  tasks:
    - name: Linux-specific tasks
      block:
        - name: Check Linux connectivity
          ping:
        
        - name: Test sudo access
          become: yes
          command: whoami
          register: sudo_test
        
        - name: Display sudo result
          debug:
            msg: "Sudo test result: {{ sudo_test.stdout }}"
      when: ansible_os_family != "Windows"
    
    - name: Windows-specific tasks
      block:
        - name: Check Windows connectivity
          win_ping:
        
        - name: Test administrative access
          win_shell: |
            $currentUser = [System.Security.Principal.WindowsIdentity]::GetCurrent()
            $principal = New-Object System.Security.Principal.WindowsPrincipal($currentUser)
            $isAdmin = $principal.IsInRole([System.Security.Principal.WindowsBuiltInRole]::Administrator)
            Write-Output "Is Administrator: $isAdmin"
          register: admin_test
        
        - name: Display admin test result
          debug:
            msg: "{{ admin_test.stdout_lines }}"
      when: ansible_os_family == "Windows"
Troubleshooting Common Issues
SSH Connection Issues
Problem: SSH connection refused Solution:

# Check SSH service
sudo systemctl status sshd

# Check SSH configuration
sudo sshd -T | grep -i port
sudo sshd -T | grep -i permitrootlogin

# Test SSH connection manually
ssh -i ~/.ssh/ansible_key ansible@target-host
Problem: Permission denied (publickey) Solution:

# Check key permissions
ls -la ~/.ssh/ansible_key*

# Verify authorized_keys on target
ssh target-host "cat ~/.ssh/authorized_keys"

# Check SSH agent
ssh-add -l
ssh-add ~/.ssh/ansible_key
WinRM Connection Issues
Problem: WinRM connection timeout Solution:

# Check WinRM service
Get-Service WinRM

# Test WinRM connectivity
Test-WSMan -ComputerName localhost

# Check firewall rules
Get-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName "*WinRM*"
Problem: Authentication failure Solution:

# Check WinRM authentication settings
winrm get winrm/config/service/auth

# Enable basic authentication if needed
winrm set winrm/config/service/auth '@{Basic="true"}'
Controller-Specific Issues
Problem: Credential not found Solution:

Verify credential exists in Resources → Credentials
Check credential permissions and organization assignment
Ensure job template references correct credential
Problem: Playbook execution fails Solution:

Check job output logs in Views → Jobs
Verify inventory host variables
Test credentials manually outside of Controller
Verification and Testing
Subtask 5.1: Create Verification Playbook
---
- name: Credential Verification Suite
  hosts: all
  gather_facts: yes
  tasks:
    - name: Collect system facts
      setup:
      register: facts
    
    - name: Create verification report
      local_action:
        module: copy
        content: |
          Credential Verification Report
          =============================
          Host: {{ inventory_hostname }}
          OS Family: {{ ansible_os_family }}
          Distribution: {{ ansible_distribution | default('N/A') }}
          Version: {{ ansible_distribution_version | default('N/A') }}
          Architecture: {{ ansible_architecture }}
          Connection Type: {{ ansible_connection }}
          User: {{ ansible_user | default(ansible_ssh_user) }}
          Timestamp: {{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }}
          
          Connection Status: SUCCESS
        dest: "./verification_{{ inventory_hostname }}.txt"
      
    - name: Display success message
      debug:
        msg: "Credential verification completed successfully for {{ inventory_hostname }}"
Subtask 5.2: Performance Testing
---
- name: Credential Performance Test
  hosts: all
  serial: 5
  tasks:
    - name: Record start time
      set_fact:
        start_time: "{{ ansible_date_time.epoch }}"
    
    - name: Execute test commands
      shell: |
        echo "Testing credential performance"
        date
        whoami
        pwd
      register: test_output
    
    - name: Record end time
      set_fact:
        end_time: "{{ ansible_date_time.epoch }}"
    
    - name: Calculate execution time
      debug:
        msg: "Execution time: {{ (end_time | int) - (start_time | int) }} seconds"
