Security Best Practices Learned
Use SSH keys instead of passwords for Linux authentication
Implement proper file permissions for SSH keys (600 for private, 644 for public)
Rotate credentials regularly to maintain security
Use Ansible Vault for storing sensitive credential data
Limit credential scope to necessary systems and users
